{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>One bull, one ram.</b> These correspond to Israel: 'Stay with Me a little longer.' This is an expression of love — like children taking leave of their father, and he says to them: 'Your departure is hard for me; stay one more day.' A parable of a king who made a feast, etc., as is found in tractate Sukkah (there). And in the midrash of Rabbi Tanchuma: The Torah teaches proper conduct — one who has a guest: on the first day he feeds him appetizers, the next day fish, the next day beef, the next day legumes, the next day vegetables — diminishing as the festival departs."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:13.647220127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}